          "judgment": "I5.4 states the decreasing-psh limit property by reference to the preceding subharmonic case; no nonexistent separate printed full proof is claimed. Its application can be reconstructed directly: on each small ball the radial truncations have a common upper bound, are psh by nonnegative nondecreasing logarithmic slopes, and decrease. Their limit is usc, and monotone convergence of the upper-bound-minus-potential passes every complex-line submean inequality, including the canonical minus-infinity value at the pole. I5.8's whole positive-Hessian representative proof was read. The smooth radial Hessian criterion explicitly allows semipositivity, so density zeros require no strict Hessian assumption."
