          "judgment": "The complete bounded corrected expansion and Proposition2.1 proof, including positivity by closed local approximations and the epsilon limit, were reread. Its antecedent is Ti>=0, so the new semipositive radial current at a smooth density zero is admitted. On compact finite-level subsets the actual potential is bounded, exact locality identifies the ordinary radial determinant, and exclusion of the pole plus the explicit integrable density gives mass one. Conditional product truncations are actual pullbacks; dimensions leave exactly binomial(m+k,m)h0^m wedge q kappa^k, and multiplying by the strict superlevel removes boundary-level contributions. No Section2.2 unbounded theorem, BMP, global exact Hermitian smoothing or mass invariance for nonclosed backgrounds is imported."
